WHAT WAS TESTED
Re-ran plan todo 3 PostCompact raw-pipe QA with a scratch cwd OUTSIDE the worktree that actually contains project rules, so the post-compact recovery path has something to inject and the 600k vs 200k budgets are exercised.

Previous run used the worktree as cwd with no always-apply project rules. PostCompact stdout was empty for all three models; the compact SessionStart follow-up then injected only bundled Hephaestus bodies (18967 / 11728 / 10188) — variant size, not budget truncation.

Handler facts (read, not edited):
- runPostCompactHook only markSessionCompacted (clears staticDedup, sets postCompactPending) and returns "".
- withPostCompactBudget runs on the next SessionStart source=compact / UserPromptSubmit recovery.
- Project rules are discovered from CONTEXT.md and .omo/rules (alwaysApply: true). There is no .codex/rules source.
- Bundled Hephaestus is never-truncated and differs by model, so it was excluded via CODEX_RULES_ENABLED_SOURCES so budget truncation is the thing being measured.
- Default postCompactMaxResultChars=4000. 760_000-byte retained transcript → unknown-model dynamic budget floors at 500; gpt-6-astra / gpt-5.6-sol stay at the 4000 cap (600k/650k windows still have room).

