WHAT WAS OBSERVED
PostCompact CLI stdout is empty for every model (implementation: mark compacted, return "").
The budgeted rules guide is emitted by SessionStart source=compact after that mark, as a mandatory read-directive of project rule paths truncated by withPostCompactBudget.
With 80 large always-apply rules + CONTEXT.md and a 760k retained transcript, astra and sol keep the 4000-class directive (31 listing lines) and unknown is cut to 1 path (665 chars).

WHY THIS IS ENOUGH
The previous empty-JSON result was lack of project rules, not a missing PostCompact emitter. Inputs were adjusted (scratch project + large always-apply rules + compacted 760k transcript + SessionStart prime); no production code was changed. The three non-zero recovery lengths show astra≈sol (600k class) > unknown-model (200k fallback, truncated). Real ~/.codex/config.toml shasum unchanged.

WHAT WAS OMITTED
No bun test / bun run test:* (forbidden on this machine). No agentic probes. No edits to packages/shared-skills or the main checkout. Bundled Hephaestus was not part of this probe (CODEX_RULES_ENABLED_SOURCES) because never-truncated variant bodies would re-mask the budget the way the previous 18967/11728/10188 lengths did. Isolated CODEX_HOME / scratch cwd were removed by cqa_cleanup after capture.
